They also argue that the South Korean military, which was heavily armed and trained by the United States, was itching for a fight and was the one that took the initiative to cross the 38th parallel and invade North Korea. In this view, the North Korean army's response was purely defensive, as it was trying to protect its territory and people from the South Korean aggression.

